class.description:
The Poki plugin puts a web game on Poki (poki.com). Its SDK is loaded by the exported page (the plugin's [code]web_head[/code]), and the plugin is the [code]poki[/code] provider of [Services]: the game asks for its ads, game events, share links, analytics and player there, the same calls as with any other service.
[codeblock]
async fn on_revive_pressed() {
	# Poki's rewarded break, through Services.
	if await Services.rewarded_break() {
		print("Revived")
	}
}
[/codeblock]
[Services] sends the game events by itself ([code]gameLoadingFinished[/code] when the main scene is ready, [code]gameplayStart[/code] at the player's first input, stop and start around pauses and ads), mutes the game and ignores its input during an ad, as Poki asks. The plugin also keeps the arrows, the space bar and the wheel from scrolling the page around the game.
This singleton has the rest of Poki's SDK. Outside a web game (the editor, a desktop build) it is there and does nothing, and [Services] plays its test ads instead. To try the game on Poki before sending it, upload the exported folder to the Poki Inspector (https://inspector.poki.dev).
